  "steps": [
    "Preheat oven to 475°F. Dice poblano, tomato. Slice scallions. Drain beans, reserving the liquid. Thinly slice the chili. Set aside 1/2 tsp of the Southwest spice for the crema.",
    "Sauté poblano in half the oil until softened. Add tomato, scallion whites, half the beans, bean liquid, and the remaining spice.",
    "Cook the remaining beans in the rest of the oil 2-3 min, add 3 tbsp bean liquid, then stir in the butter and mash until smooth.",
    "Spread tortillas with mashed beans and filling. Roll up, place seam-down in baking dish.",
    "Top with salsa and cheese. Bake on top rack 3-5 minutes until bubbly.",
    "Mix sour cream with reserved spice and warm water for crema. Drizzle over enchiladas and top with scallion greens and chili."
